  "goodToKnow": "Die Sonne is feminine in German, unlike in many other languages! In der Sonne liegen means to lie in the sun. Sonnenbrand is sunburn, and Sonnencreme is sun cream. Sonntag (Sunday) means 'sun day'. Germans flock outdoors as soon as the Sonne appears in spring."
